{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/853654-possible-hack-selective-eidetic-memory-for-demons","id":853654,"title":"[Possible Hack] Selective Eidetic Memory For Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-26T13:43:07-07:00","id":853654,"title":"[Possible Hack] Selective Eidetic Memory For Demons","content":"<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=853613#post853613\">Here's how I would do it.</a></b> Do you think this would have too much impact in your game? I haven't figured out the crunch, but I want to be generous with the amount of information they can store. The full blown Advanced and Epic versions would be part of the Angelic psyche. That is, it'd be among those other systems that become damaged or inefficient during the Fall. This emphasizes the eerie quasi-perfection of Angels, and makes Demons more human, or at least more fallible.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Demons could selectively use the Epic version after they reach a certain level of Primum without the need to purchase it separately, if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-26-2016, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T13:52:45-07:00","id":853660,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that this would just grossly overcomplicate an already potentially frustrating scenario. I don't know about you, but I find memory rolls are not super common, and can be extremely frustrating if a character cannot recall something his player recalls clearly. From my own experience Eidetic Memory mostly gets used exactly as you describe, to memorize a page at a glance, or steal someone's pin number. The only difference being that the player doesn't have to keep a conscious list of memories, which frankly just seems like a boat of extra bookkeeping with no appreciable benefit.<br /> <br /> Is Eidetic Memory really something you've struggled with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T14:06:25-07:00","id":853669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/853654-possible-hack-selective-eidetic-memory-for-demons?p=853660#post853660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that this would just grossly overcomplicate an already potentially frustrating scenario. I don't know about you, but I find memory rolls are not super common, and can be extremely frustrating if a character cannot recall something his player recalls clearly. From my own experience Eidetic Memory mostly gets used exactly as you describe, to memorize a page at a glance, or steal someone's pin number. The only difference being that the player doesn't have to keep a conscious list of memories, which frankly just seems like a boat of extra bookkeeping with no appreciable benefit.<br /> <br /> Is Eidetic Memory really something you've struggled with?</div> </div> </div> </div> You have a very good point. It was mostly a role playing consideration. I had a hard time imagining how someone could mess up anything but the most ludicrously complex recollection with a memory like that.<br /> <br /> I think I might be running into the same pitfall I did when I expressed my concern that Knowing and Unveiling could make certain conflicts too easy. It really is better to ST it right than to come up with a crippling house rule.<br /> <br /> If I do go through with this, I should write something simple.<br /> <br /> <b>*brain audibly grinds and hisses to overcome the crunch obsession*</b><br /> <br /> Spend 1 Aether as an instant action to remove a memory. This triggers Aetheric Resonance.<br /> <br /> There.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You know what? I was probably assuming too much. If Demons don't go off the deep end every day, their memories are probably modular enough to handle this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-26-2016, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T15:29:47-07:00","id":853708,"title":"","content":"There's a passage in Flowers of Hell that I considered one of the weaker parts of that book, where it imputes a strange and intense neurosis on all of the Unchained based on having clear memories, as if they were constantly actively reliving every individual memory, at full emotional intensity. It always seemed destructive to the game, and to make little diegetic sense to boot. I don't know of any human being who recalls memories at full blast all the time like that. It could be made a way in which the demonic mind supercedes the memory of a human with Eidetic Memory, but... why would you want it to? It doesn't even line up with the behavior of demons as described in the books, really.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Remembering more things is not a handicap, in my book. It can mean being aware of more harsh truths, and that has an emotional impact, sure. But it doesn't somehow shut off the ability to heal and move on. Eidetic sense memory doesn't duplicate endorphins; you get the same emotional distance from the original experience that a clear human memory would provide, no more, no less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T23:54:19-07:00","id":853923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/853654-possible-hack-selective-eidetic-memory-for-demons?p=853708#post853708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a passage in Flowers of Hell that I considered one of the weaker parts of that book, where it imputes a strange and intense neurosis on all of the Unchained based on having clear memories, as if they were constantly actively reliving every individual memory, at full emotional intensity. It always seemed destructive to the game, and to make little diegetic sense to boot. I don't know of any human being who recalls memories at full blast all the time like that. It could be made a way in which the demonic mind supercedes the memory of a human with Eidetic Memory, but... why would you want it to? It doesn't even line up with the behavior of demons as described in the books, really.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Remembering more things is not a handicap, in my book. It can mean being aware of more harsh truths, and that has an emotional impact, sure. But it doesn't somehow shut off the ability to heal and move on. Eidetic sense memory doesn't duplicate endorphins; you get the same emotional distance from the original experience that a clear human memory would provide, no more, no less.</div> </div> </div> </div> Bingo. That is the sort of relentless pain that I thought Demons would have. You expressed it quite well. Demons tend to be more objective about the past, since they don't develop fake or distorted memories. That's pretty much it. What follows from that is up to the Demon in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T01:00:15-07:00","id":853931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/853654-possible-hack-selective-eidetic-memory-for-demons?p=853708#post853708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a passage in Flowers of Hell that I considered one of the weaker parts of that book, where it imputes a strange and intense neurosis on all of the Unchained based on having clear memories, as if they were constantly actively reliving every individual memory, at full emotional intensity.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're referring to a single paragraph that posits that the Unchained don't tend to have the emotional content of their memories degrade over time, which is specifically something bits of the fiction have pointed to as a reason some demons choose to go back to the Machine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It could be made a way in which the demonic mind supercedes the memory of a human with Eidetic Memory, but... why would you want it to? It doesn't even line up with the behavior of demons as described in the books, really. </div> </div> </div>A little over an approximate fourth of demons with Agendas belong to a faction whose implied majority rationale for Infrastructural sabotage is a sense that God betrayed them.<br /> <br /> What it means in brief is that demons are driven for reasons beyond an abiding need for purpose. This is known.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it doesn't somehow shut off the ability to heal and move on. </div> </div> </div>Inability to forget is called out as one of the problems demons have in the STG's section on the Nightmare Labyrinth and we have an entire 1e gameline with a core mechanic built on the notion that re-experiencing emotional trauma from tangential reminders has an impact on people.<br /> <br /> The emotional distance you're talking about doesn't kick in when the Unchained recollective fidelity is a consequence of their memories essentially being non-degradable recordings bound to a pseudo-ephemeral xenocyborg whose personality axes can skew fairly far from human norms, whose control of expressions is limited only by their impulsivity, and whose vulnerability to mental tampering and the sudden manifestation of personal compulsions is often a direct function of how well-maintained their social presence is.<br /> <br /> A demon's mind is all that is definitively them. That most of the ones who last tend to be well-practiced at not letting their history overtly warp their judgment doesn't change the fact that they're equipped to be ready to account for everything that's happened to them at a moment's notice and this has an impact on the things that tend to be on their minds.<br /> <br /> Calling it a &quot;strange and intense neurosis&quot; strikes me as highly overblown.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/853654-possible-hack-selective-eidetic-memory-for-demons?p=853923#post853923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Demons tend to be more objective about the past, since they don't develop fake or distorted memories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahahaha.<br /> <br /> Demons do not <i>naturally</i> develop fake or distorted memories. This provides them with nothing in the way of higher discernment in emotional situations or misdirection not rooted in Machine-baffles. Grudges and nostalgia are stock-in-trade for the two most active groups of demons in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T01:10:59-07:00","id":853934,"title":"","content":"Fair points, Satchel. I need to think more about this if I'm going to play a Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}